{"title":"New York City ARML","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>New York City ARML</b> team competes at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=New_York_State_Math_League\" title=\"New York State Math League\">New York State Math League</a> against other teams from New York State and at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League\" title=\"American Regions Mathematics League\">American Regions Mathematics League</a> against teams from around North America and Taiwan.  NYSML and ARML are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition\" title=\"Mathematics competition\">mathematics competitions</a> intended primarily for high school students.  The NYC team has won NYSML for all 35 years (since 1973) the contest has existed and has won more ARML championships than any other team, including ARML 2008.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=New_York_City_ARML&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.nycmathteam.org/\">NYC ARML homepage</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=New_York_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"New York mathematics competitions\">New York mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML_historical_results\" title=\"ARML historical results\">ARML historical results</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018001116\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal tim